&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVIDIA Corp&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a data-ticker=&#34;NVDA&#34; data-exchange=&#34;NASDAQ&#34; href=&#34;https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; class=&#34;ticker-link&#34;&gt;(NASDAQ:NVDA)&lt;/a&gt; reported financial results for the third quarter of fiscal 2027 after the closing bell on Tuesday, marking the company&amp;#8217;s first report without founder and former CEO &lt;strong&gt;Jensen Huang&lt;/strong&gt;, who &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63354833/jensen-huang-nvidia-return&#34;&gt;stepped down&lt;/a&gt; last week. Here&amp;#8217;s a look at the key details &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA/earnings-forecasts&#34;&gt;from the quarter&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;ul class=&#34;wp-block-list&#34;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nvidia shares are trending after earnings. &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Where is NVDA stock going?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;



&lt;h2 class=&#34;wp-block-heading&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nvidia Q3 Earnings Highlights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;Nvidia posted third-quarter revenue of $115.84 billion, beating analyst estimates of $109.08 billion, according to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.benzinga.com/pro/register-3&#34;&gt;Benzinga Pro&lt;/a&gt;. The AI chip giant reported adjusted earnings of $2.68 per share for the quarter, beating estimates of $2.48 per share. &lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;Total revenue was up 103% on a year-over-year basis. Here&amp;#8217;s a breakdown of revenue by segment. &lt;/p&gt;



&lt;ul class=&#34;wp-block-list&#34;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Center:&lt;/strong&gt; $107.6 billion, up 110% year-over-year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;



&lt;ul class=&#34;wp-block-list&#34;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edge Computing&lt;/strong&gt;: $8.2 billion, up 42% year-over-year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;&amp;#8220;Our momentum is real. Nvidia is an exceptional technology leader, powered by the relentless innovation of our people. Vera Rubin is off to an explosive start, our roadmap is on track and our ambition has never been greater,&amp;#8221; said &lt;strong&gt;Colette Kress&lt;/strong&gt;, interim CEO, executive vice president and CFO of Nvidia.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;Gross margins were 74.8% (74.9% adjusted) in the third quarter, versus 75% in the second quarter. Nvidia ended the quarter with $29.09 billion in total cash and cash equivalents. &lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;Nvidia said it returned approximately $28.1 billion to shareholders via repurchases and dividends in the quarter. The board approved a $150 billion increase to the company&amp;#8217;s repurchase authorization in September. The company had $227.3 billion remaining under its buyback at quarter&amp;#8217;s end. &lt;/p&gt;



&lt;h2 class=&#34;wp-block-heading&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&amp;#8217;s Next For Nvidia?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;Nvidia expects fourth-quarter revenue of $130 billion, plus or minus 3%, versus estimates of $125.16 billion. Gross margins are expected to be between 71% and 72% in the fourth quarter. &lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;Nvidia will pay a quarterly dividend of 25 cents per share on Dec. 23 to shareholders of record as of Dec. 2.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nvidia management will further discuss the quarter on an earnings call at 5 p.m. ET. A link to the call has been provided below.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;h2 class=&#34;wp-block-heading&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVDA Shares Rise After Earnings&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;p class=&#34;wp-block-paragraph&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVDA Price Action:&lt;/strong&gt; Nvidia shares were up 2.41% in after-hours on Tuesday, trading at $159.20 at the time of publication, according to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.benzinga.com/pro/register-3&#34;&gt;Benzinga Pro&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;



